WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:07.139
BEN WEDEMAN: Land once lush
and productive is drying up.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.643
In the delta of Italy's
once mighty river Po,

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.146
drought has struck.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.613 line:8%
FEDERICA VIDALI:
[non-english speech]

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.549 line:8%
BEN WEDEMAN: 70% of
the crop is gone,

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.718 line:14%
Frederica Vidali tells me.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:22.355
If it doesn't rain, you can
see the plants are burning up.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.493
But this year the
rains didn't come.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.896
It's Italy's worst
drought in 70 years.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.266
Her soya crop is all but gone.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.870
The drought has impacted a
third of Italy's agriculture.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:41.273
It didn't rain much during
the winter or the spring,

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:45.712
plus Italy is going through
an unprecedented heatwave,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.615
those combined to
create the perfect storm

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.250
for Italian agriculture.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.786 line:8%
Five major food
producing Italian regions

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:56.289 line:8%
have declared a
drought emergency.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.924
ANTONIO BEZZI:
[non-english speech]

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.960 line:8%
BEN WEDEMAN: Three generations
of Antonio Bezzi's family

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.695 line:14%
have cultivated rice

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:07.166 line:8%
ANTONIO BEZZI:
[non-english speech]

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.669 line:8%
BEN WEDEMAN: We've never seen
a drought like this, he says.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.772
ANTONIO BEZZI:
[non-english speech]

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:16.576
BEN WEDEMAN: Climate change
here isn't a myth, it's reality.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.943
ANTONIO BEZZI:
[non-english speech]

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.078
BEN WEDEMAN: In
the last 10 years,

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.947
Antonio says, the
area planted with rice

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:25.418
has gone down almost 50%
as a result of drought.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.857
Close to the sea there
is water everywhere,

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.693
but not a drop to drink.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.662
In normal times this
is where the saltwater

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:41.434
reached in this river, about
three miles from the Adriatic.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.570
But now, because of the drought,
because of the low level

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:48.307
of fresh water in the
river Po, the saltwater

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:52.578
reaches about 18 miles
inland, and that is having

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:56.482
a disastrous effect on crops.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.952
RODOLFO LAURENTI:
[non-english speech]

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.654
BEN WEDEMAN: Rodolfo Laurenti
works for the local water

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:05.257
authority, which closely
monitors the flow and salinity

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.926
of water in the Po Delta.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:11.364 line:8%
RODOLFO LAURENTI:
[non-english speech]

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:14.100 line:8%
BEN WEDEMAN: The moment of
real climate crisis, he says,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.537 line:14%
is 2022.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.573
To ensure adequate
drinking water,

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:23.543
one local authority
has resorted to renting

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.980
expensive mobile
desalination plants.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.481
MONICA MANTO:
[non-english speech]

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.949 line:8%
BEN WEDEMAN:
Climate change means

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.686 line:8%
we have to be ready for
emergencies like this,

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.421 line:14%
says director Monica Manto.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:41.661
Elsewhere the little fresh
river water still available

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:45.865
is used to save at least a
portion of the rice crop.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.199
ROMANA MAGNO:
[non-english speech]

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.501 line:8%
BEN WEDEMAN: But
climate scientist,

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:52.872 line:8%
Romana Magno warns
it's too little and--

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.908 line:14%
ROMANA MAGNO: It's too late.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:03:02.414 line:8%
What we can do now is
try to reduce losses.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:05.150
BEN WEDEMAN: And as this
drought goes on the losses

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.086
will only mount.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:11.824
Ben Wedeman, CNN, in the
Po River delta, Italy.

